[h2]Fixed: the uber craft chain - mythic formulas on Normal, every reagent farmable, and thrown weapons finally drop[/h2]

[b]Four of the 42 uber craftables could not be completed by anyone.[/b] Charon's Toll, Hati, The Last Word and Sanguine Orbit each called for three Ragnarok items that this mod's database does not contain, so their recipes were dead ends no amount of farming could finish. That is fixed, along with the rest of the craft chain.

[list]
[*][b]Mythic Formulas can now drop on Normal.[/b] All 42 uber formulas sat only on the Epic and Legendary tables, so a Normal character reached exactly none of them. They now appear on all four Normal act tables at about 1.5 percent of a formula roll, deliberately rarer than the base game already makes them on Epic (2 percent) and Legendary (5 percent). Normal coverage goes from 0 of 42 to 42 of 42.
[*][b]Legendary items still do not drop on Normal.[/b] This was an exemption for formulas only, and formulas are common-grade items, so no legendary gear moved. Measured: the Normal weapon branch reaches 116 items, none of them legendary.
[*][b]Every reagent is now findable by farming Legendary.[/b] 36 of the 78 reagents could not be paid by any chest: ordinary uniques stranded on base level banded tables, the Immortal Throne divine artifacts, and the three that simply do not exist here. Now 61 of 82 drop from Legendary chests, and every one of them is payable by all 19 legendary chest surfaces, so no single boss or area gates anything.
[*][b]The green Monster Infrequent items stay monster specific, on purpose.[/b] That is the one exception, and it is now verified rather than assumed: every green reagent is proven to have a live monster that drops it. One had no living carrier at all, so it was placed in chests instead.
[*][b]Legendary thrown weapons drop for the first time.[/b] Nothing in the game could pay the thrown class - there was no unique one hand ranged loot table anywhere in this era's database, so one was written. Expect roughly 1.3 thrown weapons per six chest boss run on Legendary. The four craft tier ones stay prizes at about a twentieth of that, roughly five times rarer than any specific legendary spear, because they are still meant to be crafted.
[*][b]All 42 craftables are completable now[/b], including the seven that previously had no route at all.
[*][b]Nothing was taken away.[/b] Across the whole database this update raised 18 values and lowered none, added 18 loot entries and removed none. The only replacements are the reagent lists on the four broken thrown recipes.
[*][b]A permanent gate so it cannot come back.[/b] The build now fails loudly if any craftable loses its formula, if a reagent stops being farmable from enough places, if a green's monster disappears, or if the thrown class stops paying. It is checked against twelve deliberately broken builds.
[/list]

[i]This update changes loot tables and four recipes only. No stat, skill, monster, quest or map was touched. The armour and loot distribution balance, the uber orb weapon breadth, the portal page cap, the Epic and Legendary soul names and the chest breadth work from the previous updates are all included.[/i]
